1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,117
We will move to Earth's horizon.

2
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:06,257
We will find infinity for sure.

3
00:00:06,340 --> 00:00:13,137
Let's save all this blue sea and
let the wind Take us far away!

4
00:00:13,220 --> 00:00:20,097
Don't give up.

5
00:00:20,180 --> 00:00:22,937
So I can come back to this moment.

6
00:00:23,020 --> 00:00:26,077
So I can be present right here.

7
00:00:26,160 --> 00:00:28,717
Throw away this drop.

8
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:30,177
Sometimes we share.

9
00:00:30,260 --> 00:00:31,257
Shut it up!

10
00:00:31,340 --> 00:00:34,237
Do not be so afraid to podcast.

11
00:00:34,320 --> 00:00:36,937
To have a friend right here.

12
00:00:37,020 --> 00:00:40,317
And I will always be here by your side.

13
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:43,477
To take care of you.

14
00:00:43,560 --> 00:00:46,317
Even in the darkest of times.

15
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:48,237
I'll try looking brave.

16
00:00:48,320 --> 00:00:50,257
It's alright now.

17
00:00:50,340 --> 00:00:54,017
Cause we are the ones who
are meant to rule them all.

18
00:00:54,100 --> 00:00:56,697
We will move to our same horizon.

19
00:00:56,780 --> 00:00:59,817
We will find insanity for sure.

20
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:02,537
We're a world from our head.

21
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:04,457
We will win for sure.

22
00:01:04,540 --> 00:01:05,517
Dreaming on.

23
00:01:05,600 --> 00:01:07,937
We will move to the worst day horizon.

24
00:01:08,020 --> 00:01:10,837
We will fight however we can.

25
00:01:10,920 --> 00:01:13,757
In order to be the best we will run.

26
00:01:13,840 --> 00:01:16,477
To the top, to the end.

27
00:01:16,560 --> 00:01:19,297
We gotta be the world.

28
00:01:19,380 --> 00:01:22,260
Cause just keep dreaming on.

29
00:01:23,100 --> 00:01:25,417
I just can't give up now.

30
00:01:25,500 --> 00:01:28,280
I can never stop cause.

31
00:01:28,860 --> 00:01:31,617
I gotta give everything I got to.

32
00:01:31,700 --> 00:01:35,380
Think of the greatest of all times.

33
00:01:36,220 --> 00:01:39,097
We will move towards the horizon.

34
00:01:39,180 --> 00:01:42,357
We will find infinite fortunes.

35
00:01:42,440 --> 00:01:44,637
We will step ahead.

36
00:01:44,720 --> 00:01:46,697
We will wait for sure.

37
00:01:46,780 --> 00:01:48,980
So keep moving on.

38
00:01:56,860 --> 00:01:57,720
Whoa!

39
00:02:06,500 --> 00:02:08,700
Move in and capture Straw Hat Luffy!

40
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:12,330
Bring it on!

41
00:02:15,260 --> 00:02:16,660
Channel the Hock!

42
00:02:18,500 --> 00:02:19,735
Blow through my body!

43
00:02:21,080 --> 00:02:22,580
I got you!

44
00:02:29,280 --> 00:02:30,110
No!

45
00:02:32,420 --> 00:02:34,320
I'm gonna send you to hell!

46
00:02:43,300 --> 00:02:44,980
Man, I was still off!

47
00:02:45,560 --> 00:02:47,160
How did I do it?

48
00:02:49,460 --> 00:02:52,897
Hitting Kaido with Haki from
the outside isn't gonna cut it!

49
00:02:52,980 --> 00:02:54,700
I can't just hit the target.

50
00:02:54,860 --> 00:02:56,742
I have to let Haki flow into it.

51
00:02:59,640 --> 00:03:01,760
It's not power, it's control.

52
00:03:02,240 --> 00:03:04,697
Kaido's scales are too
tough to just punch.

53
00:03:04,780 --> 00:03:07,192
This is the only way I can break through.

54
00:03:07,860 --> 00:03:09,980
Crap, it's still way too much.

55
00:03:10,540 --> 00:03:12,100
Don't screw with me.

56
00:03:19,760 --> 00:03:22,080
That punch didn't feel right either.

57
00:03:23,500 --> 00:03:24,330
Come here!

58
00:03:25,880 --> 00:03:28,821
Need you guys to line up
so I can figure this out!

59
00:03:29,640 --> 00:03:31,320
I'll master Ryo and Knight!

60
00:03:31,960 --> 00:03:32,790
Let's go!

61
00:03:35,940 --> 00:03:38,000
That thing gets Mr. Straw Hat down.

62
00:03:38,440 --> 00:03:39,540
Look at him go!

63
00:03:40,340 --> 00:03:42,397
Chopper Emon, shall we make our way down?

64
00:03:42,480 --> 00:03:43,310
Uh-huh!

65
00:03:43,393 --> 00:03:44,811
Let's go and rescue Olin!

66
00:03:45,280 --> 00:03:46,110
Huh?

67
00:03:46,193 --> 00:03:47,023
Rescue who now?

68
00:03:47,140 --> 00:03:48,493
Forget about that lady!

69
00:03:48,720 --> 00:03:50,417
In fact, I'm glad that we lost her!

70
00:03:50,500 --> 00:03:52,180
Loopy Daddy needs help.

71
00:03:52,460 --> 00:03:53,401
Leave her, Kiku.

72
00:03:53,720 --> 00:03:57,560
Why isn't he trying to run
yet? Let's go! All right.

73
00:03:58,400 --> 00:04:00,518
Warden, what if the prisoners rebel?

74
00:04:00,940 --> 00:04:04,197
Shouldn't we get them back in
their cells while we still can?

75
00:04:04,280 --> 00:04:05,300
Get on it.

76
00:04:07,100 --> 00:04:08,120
I'm impressed.

77
00:04:08,340 --> 00:04:09,477
He's sticking it to him.

78
00:04:09,560 --> 00:04:11,620
He's crazy strong. It's unreal.

79
00:04:11,900 --> 00:04:13,957
I'm thinking we should
make a break for it.

80
00:04:14,040 --> 00:04:14,870
Right.

81
00:04:14,953 --> 00:04:16,217
Most of the guards have taken off.

82
00:04:16,300 --> 00:04:17,300
Now's our chance.

83
00:04:17,880 --> 00:04:19,420
I know what to do.

84
00:04:20,040 --> 00:04:22,057
One poison drives out another, right?

85
00:04:22,140 --> 00:04:23,720
Go and get ready, Difugo.

86
00:04:23,920 --> 00:04:27,120
I'm making the call. Oh, yeah? You sure?

87
00:04:27,520 --> 00:04:28,500
All right.

88
00:04:32,240 --> 00:04:34,500
Attention, inmates! Listen up!

89
00:04:34,760 --> 00:04:35,760
This is an order!

90
00:04:36,020 --> 00:04:40,373
Your friend Lufitato is a wild animal
who wants to tear this prison apart.

91
00:04:40,560 --> 00:04:42,854
And you are going to bring him to heal.

92
00:04:43,860 --> 00:04:45,720
What's that guy talking about?

93
00:04:49,640 --> 00:04:55,600
If you still refuse to fall in line,
you all know what comes next. Boo!

94
00:04:57,220 --> 00:04:58,050
Go!

95
00:04:58,133 --> 00:05:01,817
If you want to live through this,
then capture Luffy Toto this instant!

96
00:05:01,900 --> 00:05:02,730
Oh, come on!

97
00:05:02,813 --> 00:05:04,397
Do you actually think that this will work?

98
00:05:04,480 --> 00:05:06,715
These guys aren't gonna listen to you!

99
00:05:17,120 --> 00:05:18,920
Stop it! Let me go!

100
00:05:19,420 --> 00:05:20,797
Don't you want to ask him?

101
00:05:20,880 --> 00:05:23,200
I want your side, you bunch of dopes!

102
00:05:23,580 --> 00:05:25,857
Listen, it's not like we're
rooting for the guards here.

103
00:05:25,940 --> 00:05:28,857
We don't want to do this, but
we don't have much of a choice.

104
00:05:28,940 --> 00:05:31,677
We've got our hopes up that
we saw you fight back there.

105
00:05:31,760 --> 00:05:34,277
But even if we do manage
to break out of here,

106
00:05:34,360 --> 00:05:37,066
Orochi's still in charge,
so what's the point?

107
00:05:39,560 --> 00:05:43,817
Besides that, we already tried to revenge
Lord Odin once and ended up in here.

108
00:05:43,900 --> 00:05:46,020
That bastard Kaido's way too tough.

109
00:05:46,240 --> 00:05:48,537
Plus, we've lost our
families and comrades, too.

110
00:05:48,620 --> 00:05:52,326
He's beaten us into submission
with little hope for the future.

111
00:05:53,880 --> 00:05:55,900
Seeing you fight back was amazing,

112
00:05:56,160 --> 00:06:00,748
but Lord Yasui's execution brought back
all that fear and despair from before.

113
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:03,317
Even if we do manage to break out of here,

114
00:06:03,400 --> 00:06:06,257
what's the point when we'll
just be homeless and starving?

115
00:06:06,340 --> 00:06:08,960
The people of Wano will
never be free again,

116
00:06:09,160 --> 00:06:11,572
so we might as well just give up already.

117
00:06:13,960 --> 00:06:15,000
Wise decision.

118
00:06:15,380 --> 00:06:17,357
You'll obey us if you don't want to die.

119
00:06:17,440 --> 00:06:20,220
Just let them go, you selfish jerk!

120
00:06:20,480 --> 00:06:22,860
You're the one who's being selfish! Huh?

121
00:06:23,160 --> 00:06:26,757
As an outsider from overseas, you
can run and fight all you like.

122
00:06:26,840 --> 00:06:28,377
but that's your choice to make!

123
00:06:28,460 --> 00:06:31,500
You can't expect us to
back you up! We're tired!

124
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:34,880
Please, have mercy!

125
00:06:35,240 --> 00:06:36,840
Don't give us false hope!

126
00:06:37,200 --> 00:06:38,640
That's just so cruel!

127
00:06:43,580 --> 00:06:44,660
You guys!

128
00:06:49,540 --> 00:06:50,599
Are you all right?

129
00:06:50,700 --> 00:06:52,700
We're going to get you help, okay?

130
00:06:55,640 --> 00:06:56,470
Really?

131
00:06:56,553 --> 00:06:57,383
You sure about that?

132
00:06:57,466 --> 00:07:00,137
I think you should worry more
about yourself than each other.

133
00:07:00,220 --> 00:07:01,680
I'm burning! It's hot!

134
00:07:01,880 --> 00:07:03,757
Someone help me! Hang on.

135
00:07:03,840 --> 00:07:05,252
You're going to be fine.

136
00:07:08,380 --> 00:07:09,697
What's this green crab?

137
00:07:09,780 --> 00:07:12,721
I told you what happened
if you stepped out alive.

138
00:07:12,860 --> 00:07:15,897
What I just fired at you was
a highly contagious play.

139
00:07:15,980 --> 00:07:18,509
One touch and you're
going to get infected.

140
00:07:24,100 --> 00:07:27,317
Let those poor bastards
serve as an example in case

141
00:07:27,400 --> 00:07:30,635
the rest of you decide you
want to try something funny.

142
00:07:31,460 --> 00:07:35,342
You see, Master Queen has a hobby
of creating weapons and viruses.

143
00:07:36,040 --> 00:07:38,334
This is just a taste of what he can do.

144
00:07:41,140 --> 00:07:42,040
It's burning.

145
00:07:43,320 --> 00:07:49,000
these are master queen's special
playgrounds who else wants to test them out

146
00:07:54,060 --> 00:07:56,717
Straw Hat i can't help but wonder why you

147
00:07:56,800 --> 00:07:58,657
thought the prisoners
would ever rally behind

148
00:07:58,740 --> 00:08:02,157
you their will to resist dried up long ago

149
00:08:02,240 --> 00:08:05,757
and you're about to suffer
along with them like

150
00:08:05,840 --> 00:08:08,317
hell i am i dare you to try and shoot me

151
00:08:08,400 --> 00:08:11,017
didn't you hear what i
said you can get infected

152
00:08:11,100 --> 00:08:13,597
by those around you
even if i don't hit you

153
00:08:13,680 --> 00:08:17,820
everyone listen you guys gotta spread out

154
00:08:18,540 --> 00:08:24,737
what does it matter so what if we die
here maybe it's for the best i can't

155
00:08:24,820 --> 00:08:30,280
explain right now but trust me i can fix
things for you say your prayers Straw Hat

156
00:08:36,660 --> 00:08:37,940
Don't hold back,

157
00:08:38,120 --> 00:08:43,157
Straw Hat Boy Be their beacon of hope
Let them know the fire of rebellion

158
00:08:43,240 --> 00:08:48,960
still burns We've been given one
last chance Kaido can be defeated

159
00:08:53,680 --> 00:08:57,177
I heard a voice coming from
the never-opening cell Guess

160
00:08:57,260 --> 00:09:00,520
he's still kicking after all
There's a person in there?

161
00:09:00,660 --> 00:09:02,131
I thought it was a beast.

162
00:09:02,520 --> 00:09:03,357
I forgot.

163
00:09:03,440 --> 00:09:05,322
No one told you what was inside.

164
00:09:05,880 --> 00:09:10,115
It's no man and it's no animal, but
it's proven to be quite the monster.

165
00:09:10,280 --> 00:09:12,597
The plan was to keep
feeding him fish from the

166
00:09:12,680 --> 00:09:15,717
factory's polluted water
runoff until he died in agony.

167
00:09:15,800 --> 00:09:20,400
But he was quite resilient, as those
orders came from the Shogun 13 years ago.

168
00:09:21,180 --> 00:09:25,420
It was intended to be a slow and
painful death, but he hung on.

169
00:09:26,060 --> 00:09:29,540
Honestly, we let this
go on for far too long.

170
00:09:30,460 --> 00:09:36,060
The prisoner inside of that cell is
none other than one of the Akazaya Nine!

171
00:09:36,720 --> 00:09:37,880
Are you joking?

172
00:09:38,120 --> 00:09:40,497
But I thought they all died out long ago.

173
00:09:40,580 --> 00:09:41,880
Finish the job!

174
00:09:42,060 --> 00:09:44,060
We'll call it an accidental death!

175
00:09:44,900 --> 00:09:45,800
That laugh!

176
00:09:46,880 --> 00:09:49,140
No question, it's Kawamatsu!

177
00:09:50,760 --> 00:09:51,800
Wait for me!

178
00:09:52,700 --> 00:09:53,900
I'm on my way!

179
00:09:54,880 --> 00:09:56,940
Would you take a look at this guy?

180
00:09:57,080 --> 00:10:00,609
That slimy little freak is a
member of the famous Akazaya 9?

181
00:10:02,180 --> 00:10:03,900
He's mine, boys!

182
00:10:07,220 --> 00:10:08,640
You tricked me!

183
00:10:10,600 --> 00:10:12,300
The hell? A needle?

184
00:10:12,500 --> 00:10:13,940
Maybe a fishbone?

185
00:10:15,820 --> 00:10:17,760
Slime will protect me!

186
00:10:23,960 --> 00:10:25,360
This is bad.

187
00:10:25,840 --> 00:10:27,317
The huge-headed guy got away.

188
00:10:27,400 --> 00:10:28,230
Kabatsu!

189
00:10:29,520 --> 00:10:31,755
Your keys and your sword are incoming!

190
00:10:38,380 --> 00:10:40,800
Impeccable timing. I'm grateful.

191
00:10:46,060 --> 00:10:49,940
Been far too long, my trusty old blade.

192
00:10:51,320 --> 00:10:52,150
Sotomousso.

193
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:54,080
So tell me.

194
00:10:58,780 --> 00:11:01,040
Do you like sumo wrestling?

195
00:11:07,300 --> 00:11:08,140
Kawamatsu!

196
00:11:08,460 --> 00:11:09,540
Don't worry.

197
00:11:09,860 --> 00:11:10,780
I'm on my way.

198
00:11:11,020 --> 00:11:12,240
Everyone ready?

199
00:11:14,100 --> 00:11:15,720
Here I go!

200
00:11:19,040 --> 00:11:19,880
Akariwa!

201
00:11:22,080 --> 00:11:22,910
Ah!

202
00:11:27,340 --> 00:11:29,140
Oh, what the hell?

203
00:11:29,620 --> 00:11:31,360
Still just as tough.

204
00:11:31,860 --> 00:11:35,680
Remember, Kawamatsu, you lose
if your feet leave the ground.

205
00:11:39,120 --> 00:11:40,597
That technique...

206
00:11:40,680 --> 00:11:41,820
things were.

207
00:11:43,360 --> 00:11:44,520
Gotcha now!

208
00:11:44,960 --> 00:11:48,740
A flash of steel at the
blowing rapids of a river.

209
00:11:54,180 --> 00:11:56,900
They call it Kappa style.

210
00:11:59,520 --> 00:12:01,920
River of Retribution!

211
00:12:16,320 --> 00:12:20,157
Do you think I found those
poisonous fish a delicacy?

212
00:12:20,240 --> 00:12:24,593
No, rather they were so vile that my
innards twisted and begged for mercy.

213
00:12:24,680 --> 00:12:28,320
Yet, I stood firm for 13 years.

214
00:12:28,640 --> 00:12:32,037
Compared to my lord's suffering,
it was barely a drop in a pond.

215
00:12:32,120 --> 00:12:34,780
Long have I waited, but the time has come.

216
00:12:35,120 --> 00:12:38,240
Kawamatsu the Kappa has
joined this epic crusade.

217
00:12:44,540 --> 00:12:45,370
Kawamatsu!

218
00:12:46,660 --> 00:12:47,490
Kiku! Ugh.

219
00:12:49,520 --> 00:12:51,340
You haven't changed a bit.

220
00:12:51,900 --> 00:12:54,060
I'm so glad that you are free.

221
00:12:54,760 --> 00:12:56,900
Raizo, same to you. Huh?

222
00:12:57,320 --> 00:12:58,760
Kiku, you're here too?

223
00:12:59,040 --> 00:13:00,060
What's going on?

224
00:13:00,240 --> 00:13:03,317
Anyone know who the short
guy with a swollen head is?

225
00:13:03,400 --> 00:13:04,800
He's an intruder, sir.

226
00:13:05,040 --> 00:13:08,777
The man who stole the sword and cup
keys, I don't know how he got in here.

227
00:13:08,860 --> 00:13:10,540
Hey, don't just stand there.

228
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:13,180
Do something about him, sir.

229
00:13:25,140 --> 00:13:26,580
I gave you orders.

230
00:13:26,880 --> 00:13:28,704
Why the heck did you turn back?

231
00:13:29,260 --> 00:13:30,090
Kawamatsu.

232
00:13:30,220 --> 00:13:31,573
Are you feeling better?

233
00:13:31,760 --> 00:13:32,760
Get it all out.

234
00:13:34,120 --> 00:13:35,160
My apologies.

235
00:13:35,580 --> 00:13:37,520
That was 13 years of bad fish.

236
00:13:41,780 --> 00:13:44,000
Get the playgrounds ready to fire!

237
00:13:44,300 --> 00:13:46,557
Finish them off before
this gets out of hand!

238
00:13:46,640 --> 00:13:49,117
Everyone prepare for battle!

239
00:13:49,200 --> 00:13:53,497
I demand you release Sir Luffy!

240
00:13:53,580 --> 00:13:54,917
Daddy Oh kiku!

241
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:55,830
Rise!

242
00:13:55,913 --> 00:14:01,017
Oh hey!

243
00:14:01,100 --> 00:14:06,777
Don't tell me your boss yogurt!

244
00:14:06,860 --> 00:14:07,977
Oh I am!

245
00:14:08,060 --> 00:14:11,317
However, it's you who should speak up!

246
00:14:11,400 --> 00:14:14,757
Why don't you tell them
who you really are?

247
00:14:14,840 --> 00:14:19,297
If you want to inspire
those with broken spirits,

248
00:14:19,380 --> 00:14:23,037
you must remove your disguise
and reveal your identities!

249
00:14:23,120 --> 00:14:28,217
They once fought for our cause, so
I'm certain their passion will return!

250
00:14:28,300 --> 00:14:30,157
How true!

251
00:14:30,240 --> 00:14:32,337
Splendid idea!

252
00:14:32,420 --> 00:14:34,477
I agree as well!

253
00:14:34,560 --> 00:14:37,137
Let's earn their trust before proceeding!

254
00:14:37,220 --> 00:14:40,477
Listen close!

255
00:14:40,560 --> 00:14:42,877
We are not mere ghosts or memories!

256
00:14:42,960 --> 00:14:45,380
The legends are true!

257
00:15:09,980 --> 00:15:12,080
No way! That mask!

258
00:15:12,580 --> 00:15:16,080
It belongs to the most beautiful
swordsman in all of Wano.

259
00:15:16,620 --> 00:15:18,660
I thought he died at Oden Castle.

260
00:15:19,180 --> 00:15:22,400
Could it really be Kiku
Nojo of the Fallen Snow?

261
00:15:24,180 --> 00:15:25,010
Huh?

262
00:15:25,093 --> 00:15:26,160
Wait, you're a guy?

263
00:15:26,440 --> 00:15:28,420
I am a woman at my heart.

264
00:15:28,740 --> 00:15:30,100
The mask, yikes!

265
00:15:31,280 --> 00:15:32,500
Hold up.

266
00:15:33,800 --> 00:15:36,880
That's Fukurokuju's rival
ninja, Raizo of the Mist.

267
00:15:37,680 --> 00:15:40,960
Samurai there is the most
powerful sumo wrestler ever.

268
00:15:41,480 --> 00:15:43,140
Yokozuna Kawamatsu!

269
00:15:43,620 --> 00:15:46,700
And the old man is who
we suspected all along.

270
00:15:47,060 --> 00:15:48,880
He's Yoguro the Flower!

271
00:15:50,640 --> 00:15:52,260
One question, though.

272
00:15:52,840 --> 00:15:55,220
Who is this Luffy Taro guy?

273
00:15:59,320 --> 00:16:01,640
Who cares about that? He is incredible!

274
00:16:02,800 --> 00:16:04,200
Hey! It's me!

275
00:16:05,580 --> 00:16:09,051
This leads me to believe Lord
Orochi's ramblings were true!

276
00:16:10,020 --> 00:16:13,200
We've got to report this
to Commander Kaido somehow!

277
00:16:13,960 --> 00:16:14,790
Nay.

278
00:16:16,160 --> 00:16:21,220
Now that you have seen us, thy
lips must be sealed forevermore.

279
00:16:25,220 --> 00:16:26,280
Now, attack!

280
00:16:30,740 --> 00:16:33,040
Nico, flower shooting kid!

281
00:16:51,540 --> 00:16:53,380
Heavy gun!

282
00:16:56,260 --> 00:16:58,260
Come, come! Got me!

283
00:17:05,440 --> 00:17:07,220
Okay, try these playgrounds.

284
00:17:10,800 --> 00:17:11,920
Oh, no.

285
00:17:16,920 --> 00:17:19,257
We keep missing him with the bullets, sir!

286
00:17:19,340 --> 00:17:20,170
What do we do?

287
00:17:20,560 --> 00:17:23,220
I told you, hit someone close to us!

288
00:17:25,260 --> 00:17:26,400
You bastards!

289
00:17:26,740 --> 00:17:27,897
Why don't you fight me?

290
00:17:27,980 --> 00:17:29,392
They've suffered enough!

291
00:17:30,340 --> 00:17:33,105
Fighting with a virus is
the lowest of the low!

292
00:17:36,280 --> 00:17:39,045
You gotta go to us first
to get to the general.

293
00:17:39,440 --> 00:17:41,560
Let's break through, chopper! On it!

294
00:17:44,020 --> 00:17:45,860
Now, gong gong!

295
00:17:47,660 --> 00:17:49,040
Heavy! He's dead!

296
00:17:54,020 --> 00:17:56,860
Leave my comrades alone!

297
00:18:06,240 --> 00:18:07,520
I second that!

298
00:18:14,240 --> 00:18:15,517
It's a demon!

299
00:18:15,600 --> 00:18:17,860
Kappa style.

300
00:18:23,200 --> 00:18:24,480
Norikiri.

301
00:18:35,080 --> 00:18:37,900
Ninpou, lightning shuriken!

302
00:18:45,600 --> 00:18:50,240
Ha ha ha ha ha.

303
00:18:51,540 --> 00:18:53,780
Ha ha ha ha.

304
00:18:54,960 --> 00:18:57,060
Ha ha ha ha ha.

305
00:18:58,040 --> 00:18:59,460
Ha ha ha.

306
00:19:00,180 --> 00:19:03,040
For you, friends of Sir Luffy.

307
00:19:03,300 --> 00:19:04,700
We're not friends.

308
00:19:05,280 --> 00:19:07,240
One of those should set you free.

309
00:19:11,120 --> 00:19:12,240
Hmm, killer.

310
00:19:19,280 --> 00:19:20,480
I've been shot!

311
00:19:21,380 --> 00:19:23,600
It burns! It burns!

312
00:19:24,920 --> 00:19:25,750
Help!

313
00:19:25,920 --> 00:19:26,920
It's some people!

314
00:19:27,300 --> 00:19:28,420
Stay away from me!

315
00:19:31,220 --> 00:19:32,920
This is pissing me off!

316
00:19:33,060 --> 00:19:35,001
The prisoners don't deserve this!

317
00:19:42,620 --> 00:19:44,577
Oh, yeah! That's right!

318
00:19:44,660 --> 00:19:48,320
You have no idea what horror awaits you.

319
00:19:51,520 --> 00:19:55,540
The plague starts with a burning
sensation from the bullet wound.

320
00:19:55,740 --> 00:20:01,720
Then the pain spreads to every corner of
your body until your blood bursts out.

321
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:07,160
The victim is left in agony, twisting
and crawling in search of relief.

322
00:20:07,680 --> 00:20:12,440
And in doing so, they infect
anyone they come in contact with.

323
00:20:14,660 --> 00:20:15,800
Ah! Ah!

324
00:20:17,640 --> 00:20:18,820
Great mercy!

325
00:20:19,500 --> 00:20:20,330
Stop!

326
00:20:20,540 --> 00:20:21,370
Ah!

327
00:20:21,880 --> 00:20:23,540
Wouldn't you look at that?

328
00:20:23,760 --> 00:20:27,040
A perfect example of
how this stuff spreads!

329
00:20:28,180 --> 00:20:29,010
Oh!

330
00:20:29,360 --> 00:20:30,300
Save me!

331
00:20:31,820 --> 00:20:32,650
Oh!

332
00:20:34,240 --> 00:20:37,740
You ever see a human being
shrivel up like that?

333
00:20:37,900 --> 00:20:40,488
They look like a bunch
of rotting old weeds!

334
00:20:53,440 --> 00:20:54,597
Do something.

335
00:20:54,680 --> 00:20:56,400
Back up or you'll infect me.

336
00:21:02,400 --> 00:21:03,560
Nice, huh?

337
00:21:04,520 --> 00:21:06,940
It's called the mummy play. Get it?

338
00:21:07,260 --> 00:21:08,600
It truly is.

339
00:21:08,760 --> 00:21:09,677
Master queens.

340
00:21:09,760 --> 00:21:11,080
Finest work!

341
00:21:18,740 --> 00:21:19,570
Go!

342
00:21:19,960 --> 00:21:22,300
Now all of you are human weapons!

343
00:21:22,780 --> 00:21:26,100
One little touch and you
can share your suffering!

344
00:21:27,840 --> 00:21:30,500
Don't take another step closer to us!

345
00:21:30,700 --> 00:21:32,700
You'll spread the virus even more!

346
00:21:33,060 --> 00:21:34,420
Just give me some time!

347
00:21:34,700 --> 00:21:36,940
I'll find a cure for you, I promise!

348
00:21:37,840 --> 00:21:39,880
Sure you want to oppose me?

349
00:21:40,140 --> 00:21:42,669
You know what happens
to rebels, don't you?

350
00:21:47,820 --> 00:21:48,650
Careful!

351
00:21:51,240 --> 00:21:53,100
Seems they have no choice.

352
00:21:53,640 --> 00:21:54,680
We're in trouble.

353
00:21:55,080 --> 00:21:58,860
All of Udon Prison is fighting against us!

354
00:22:01,040 --> 00:22:02,377
Escape all you can!

355
00:22:02,460 --> 00:22:07,957
and you shouldn't have come here.

356
00:22:08,040 --> 00:22:09,317
We don't want your help.

357
00:22:09,400 --> 00:22:12,877
None of this sort of habit now.

358
00:22:12,960 --> 00:22:14,397
We're all doomed.

359
00:22:14,480 --> 00:22:18,757
It doesn't matter if you're
the legendary Akisaya samurai.

360
00:22:18,840 --> 00:22:21,377
They outpower us in every way.

361
00:22:21,460 --> 00:22:23,037
It's pointless.

362
00:22:23,120 --> 00:22:28,077
No matter how you look
at it, you'll never win.

363
00:22:28,160 --> 00:22:29,140
Why bother?

364
00:22:30,680 --> 00:22:33,317
You're up against the worst of the worst.

365
00:22:33,400 --> 00:22:36,040
The dragon who blacks out the sky.

366
00:22:37,760 --> 00:22:40,497
Plus he has the beast
pirates to back him up.

367
00:22:40,580 --> 00:22:43,240
No one stands a chance against them.

368
00:22:46,220 --> 00:22:48,837
Please just take a look around you.

369
00:22:48,920 --> 00:22:52,657
All of this chaos unleashed
by one weapon made by.

370
00:22:52,740 --> 00:22:54,720
one of Kaido's men,

371
00:22:54,940 --> 00:23:00,940
utter devastation, utter despair,

372
00:23:01,160 --> 00:23:03,042
and Kaido never raised a finger.

373
00:23:04,420 --> 00:23:09,460
If you outsiders hadn't invaded, at least
we could have carried on with our lives.

374
00:23:09,700 --> 00:23:12,420
Even if it was miserable,
it wasn't like this.

375
00:23:12,700 --> 00:23:14,994
We weren't past the point of no return.

376
00:23:15,080 --> 00:23:17,097
We didn't have to suffer this nightmare,

377
00:23:17,180 --> 00:23:20,709
watching our own bodies shrivel
up and eat themselves alive.

378
00:23:33,900 --> 00:23:36,540
Don't touch them, Lufitaro! You'll die!

379
00:23:45,260 --> 00:23:47,840
Stop this crap right now!

380
00:23:50,040 --> 00:23:51,097
No way!

381
00:23:51,180 --> 00:23:53,000
Hey, he'll be infected too!

382
00:23:59,180 --> 00:24:01,980
You guys can't convince me!

383
00:24:09,120 --> 00:24:10,680
Is he crazy?

384
00:24:13,380 --> 00:24:16,360
Are you trying to kill yourself?

385
00:24:18,560 --> 00:24:21,560
Sarno Future, why would you do this?

386
00:24:28,160 --> 00:24:29,880
Mr. Straw Hat!

387
00:24:33,660 --> 00:24:36,380
You guys can't convince me!

388
00:24:39,760 --> 00:24:42,580
You think this tower can't be beat?

389
00:24:42,760 --> 00:24:44,220
You're just giving up!

390
00:24:45,180 --> 00:24:46,960
It can't hurt me at all!

391
00:24:47,220 --> 00:24:48,220
I'm okay!

392
00:24:48,620 --> 00:24:49,460
You see?

393
00:24:51,420 --> 00:24:52,580
Stupid liar!

394
00:24:53,080 --> 00:24:55,021
You gotta get away from this now!

395
00:24:55,280 --> 00:24:56,440
Please, Luffy!

396
00:25:04,360 --> 00:25:07,772
They're trying to break your
spirit, but you gotta listen!

397
00:25:07,980 --> 00:25:09,804
Samurai I met are really tough!

398
00:25:25,920 --> 00:25:28,100
They're fighting for you!

399
00:25:29,480 --> 00:25:31,860
Everyone has to pull together!

400
00:25:38,220 --> 00:25:40,380
You talk about your life here!

401
00:25:41,260 --> 00:25:44,880
Like slaving away for dumplings is a life.

402
00:25:47,960 --> 00:25:51,297
You give it just enough
so you don't keel over!

403
00:25:51,380 --> 00:25:54,440
You think that's what life is about?

404
00:26:08,700 --> 00:26:13,520
Look around you, a bunch of slaves.

405
00:26:13,800 --> 00:26:15,500
You're worth more!

406
00:26:21,280 --> 00:26:22,377
Huh?

407
00:26:22,460 --> 00:26:24,840
Big Bro and his friends are okay!

408
00:26:25,780 --> 00:26:26,780
Is he, though?

409
00:26:30,800 --> 00:26:33,880
And so what if I'm not
from the land of Wano?

410
00:26:35,260 --> 00:26:36,090
Big deal!

411
00:26:36,260 --> 00:26:38,920
Why is it so wrong to
get help from me, huh?

412
00:26:53,720 --> 00:26:56,480
I made a promise I got to keep.

413
00:26:59,300 --> 00:27:01,260
I have a friend named Tama.

414
00:27:01,700 --> 00:27:05,240
She made sure I could eat even
when she had nothing herself.

415
00:27:07,140 --> 00:27:10,897
So I owe it to her to make this country a

416
00:27:10,980 --> 00:27:14,040
place where she can fill
her belly every day.

417
00:27:16,200 --> 00:27:18,435
I'm going to make this a normal thing.

418
00:27:19,620 --> 00:27:22,340
I swear that by the time we leave Wano,

419
00:27:22,540 --> 00:27:26,364
it'll be a place where you can
eat as much as you want every day.

420
00:27:31,720 --> 00:27:33,980
I refuse to fail.

421
00:27:35,080 --> 00:27:38,940
Because if I do, you'll be trapped
in this living hell forever.

422
00:27:39,700 --> 00:27:41,760
Now, help me!

423
00:27:50,680 --> 00:27:53,500
I have already heard about Odin.

424
00:27:53,780 --> 00:27:55,880
Sounds like an amazing guy.

425
00:27:57,460 --> 00:28:00,560
But when Kaido killed him 20 years ago,

426
00:28:00,900 --> 00:28:04,253
everything in this country
came to a complete standstill.

427
00:28:04,380 --> 00:28:06,520
I shouldn't have to remind you.

428
00:28:11,700 --> 00:28:13,440
Trust me and my friends.

429
00:28:13,780 --> 00:28:15,040
We'll beat Kaido.

430
00:28:15,260 --> 00:28:16,780
That's why we're here.

431
00:28:18,280 --> 00:28:22,080
There's no reason for our own
allies to stand in our way!

432
00:28:28,160 --> 00:28:30,940
So make up your minds right now!

433
00:28:31,620 --> 00:28:33,600
Are you guys with us?

434
00:28:34,580 --> 00:28:36,600
Or are you with Kaido?

435
00:28:45,340 --> 00:28:47,020
You really mean it?

436
00:28:57,620 --> 00:29:00,040
Truly, you're not lying.

437
00:29:00,940 --> 00:29:03,260
You're giving this another shot.

438
00:29:18,820 --> 00:29:24,797
He's winning everyone over, that
man can sure capture a heart,

439
00:29:24,880 --> 00:29:31,397
it seems like you guys
are going weak on me, huh?

440
00:29:31,480 --> 00:29:36,337
No matter, I can still sway you to
my side with a little crowd control.

441
00:29:36,420 --> 00:29:41,897
Just one shot in the middle, then
everything will turn to chaos again.

442
00:29:41,980 --> 00:29:46,917
Time to break out the big one—how
does 200 times the amount sound?

443
00:29:47,000 --> 00:29:49,660
sound Here comes your plague shot!

444
00:29:53,420 --> 00:29:54,640
Take this!

445
00:29:55,040 --> 00:29:57,200
A plague-packed elephant smart shoe!

446
00:29:58,540 --> 00:30:00,540
Please don't do this, warden!

447
00:30:03,020 --> 00:30:04,980
Please have mercy on us!

448
00:30:05,860 --> 00:30:07,440
Mercy on us!

449
00:30:08,960 --> 00:30:12,920
Hey, Baba Nuki's going to
fire something this way. What?

450
00:30:15,360 --> 00:30:16,680
It's too late.

451
00:30:19,660 --> 00:30:21,740
Oh! Oh! Oh! Oh!

452
00:30:23,500 --> 00:30:25,080
Elephant smart shoe!

453
00:30:25,400 --> 00:30:27,780
Now sneeze smart shoe!

454
00:30:28,440 --> 00:30:29,270
Ha-ha!

455
00:30:37,200 --> 00:30:39,860
Ha-ha! No! Wait!

456
00:30:42,540 --> 00:30:44,060
Had to do it.

457
00:30:44,360 --> 00:30:46,360
The future I saw took a bad turn.

458
00:30:47,420 --> 00:30:48,320
Oh, oh!

459
00:30:49,800 --> 00:30:50,630
Oh!

460
00:30:59,140 --> 00:31:01,060
Ah, let it go, no game!

461
00:31:01,840 --> 00:31:02,670
Oh, no!

462
00:31:11,800 --> 00:31:12,630
Incredible.

463
00:31:14,740 --> 00:31:16,780
What a capable fellow!

464
00:31:19,560 --> 00:31:21,260
Handle the rest for me.

465
00:31:30,120 --> 00:31:32,560
Leave it to us. Hang on a sec.

466
00:31:32,920 --> 00:31:35,000
I'm in charge. Take it over.

467
00:31:35,560 --> 00:31:38,317
Remember what happens to
anyone who defies a jailer.

468
00:31:38,400 --> 00:31:40,777
First defense is you lose your arms.

469
00:31:40,860 --> 00:31:43,237
We know, but we don't care.

470
00:31:43,320 --> 00:31:46,320
Call us rebels, but
we've had enough of you!

471
00:31:49,200 --> 00:31:51,427
You're gonna pay for
our years of suffering!

472
00:31:51,510 --> 00:31:53,470
Get her! Yeah!

473
00:32:05,510 --> 00:32:08,610
Eight days remain before
the great battle begins.

474
00:32:09,190 --> 00:32:11,778
The enemy's main forces
are still oblivious.

475
00:32:22,350 --> 00:32:26,930
Udon has been conquered. Mr. Straw Hat!

476
00:32:27,230 --> 00:32:29,070
That was magnificent!

477
00:32:38,770 --> 00:32:42,570
I have to admit you found
one hell of an ally.

478
00:32:43,070 --> 00:32:44,750
Thank you, Kin'emon.
